{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a5b9095562d91d1a23014bb681dddf7f9f75df2a35e796434312ea1c8fe0c2cd","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan review manifest tests","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:497","src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py:_gate_commit_sha","tests/unit/test_plan_review.py:test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes","tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py:test_no_pins_preserves_legacy_manifest_bytes","tests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py:test_manifest_is_deterministic_and_path_independent","rebar.signing.gate_code_version","git status --porcelain"],"problem_keywords":["flaky test","manifest byte-equality","git dirty-state","xdist","nondeterminism","concurrent writes","monkeypatch"],"propositions":["Manifest byte-equality tests flake under pytest-xdist because gate_code_version() shells git status per call, causing -dirty suffix to flip between two build_manifest calls when a concurrent worker touches the checkout.","test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes and test_manifest_is_deterministic_and_path_independent compare manifests built in separate calls without pinning provenance, exposing a racy git-state dependency.","Monkeypatching rebar.signing.gate_code_version to a constant in affected tests eliminates the flake and is the pattern already used successfully in test_no_pins_preserves_legacy_manifest_bytes.","All manifest byte-equality test sites must pin gate_code_version to ensure deterministic equality assertions independent of concurrent filesystem mutations."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp